 81   C  TITL$NUCLEAR DATA SHEETS FOR A=81                                      
 81   c  AUTH$M. Shamsuzzoha Basunia                                            
 81   c  INST$Nuclear Science Division                                          
 81  #c       Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory                             
 81  #c       1 Cyclotron Road, Berkeley, California 94720, USA                 
 81   C  CIT$NDS 199, 271 (2025)                                                
 81   c  ABST$Nuclear structure data pertaining to all nuclei with mass number  
 81  2c  A=81 (Ni, Cu, Zn, Ga, Ge, As, Se, Br, Kr, Rb, Sr, Y, Zr, Nb, Mo) have  
 81  3c  been compiled and evaluated and incorporated into the ENSDF data file. 
 81  4c  This evaluation for A=81 supersedes the previous one, 2008Ba34.        
 81  @c  Highlights of this evaluation are the following:                       
 81  @c  From fragmentation reaction studies of {+238}U beam at 345 MeV/nucleon 
 81  2c  on a Be target, one count has been assigned to {+81}Ni in 2017Su15,    
 81  3c  which is assumed to correspond to the g.s. activity of {+81}Ni and the 
 81  4c  Adopted Levels dataset has been proposed.                              
 81  @c  The absolute I|g determined in 1982De36 ({+81}Y |e decay (70.4 s))     
 81  2c  from total I|g/total |b{++} recoils implies a 97% g.s. branch (from    
 81  3c  (5/2+) to 1/2-) in the {+81}Y |e decay, which is discrepant compared   
 81  4c  to the g.s. feeding of <2.6 in this evaluation. The absolute I|g of    
 81  5c  1982De36 was not considered in the previous evaluation (2008Ba34),     
 81  6c  same in this one as well. The reason for this major discrepancy is not 
 81  7c  understood.  The decay scheme normalization is consequently tentative. 
 81  @c  {+81}Zr g.s. half-life measurements have been reported from (113, 175, 
 81  2c  and 230|g(t)) and decay curves for |b events correlated with {+81}Zr   
 81  3c  implantations. No additional data are available. A {+81}Zr |e decay    
 81  3c  (5.3 s) dataset has been created based on the data from the Adopted    
 81  4c  Levels,Gammas of {+81}Y.                                               
 81   c  CUT$All the data received by September 1, 2024 have been evaluated.    
 81  2c  During this evaluation, the NSR database (2014Pr09) was used           
 81  3c  extensively.                                                           
 81   c  ACKN$This evaluation benefits from the previous evaluations by c.m.    
 81  2c  Baglin (2008Ba34, 1996Ba89, 1993Ba30), J. Muller (1985Mu16), and J.F.  
 81  3c  Lemming (1975Le08) and the addition of the newly identified {+81}Mo    
 81  4c  isotope data by B. Singh dated: March 31, 2015. The evaluator is       
 81  5c  thankful to the the XUNDL dataset compilers. Also the support of Ms.   
 81  6c  JoAnn Totans, NNDC, for providing secondary and other articles is      
 81  8c  deeply acknowledged. The evaluator is grateful to Dr. Jun Chen (MSU)   
 81  9c  for a critical data checking of the manuscript and for providing many  
 81  ac  useful comments/suggestions.  Finally, the evaluator is thankful to    
 81  bc  Dr. E. McCutchan (NNDC, BNL) for the editorial comments and the follow 
 81  cc  up process to publish the manuscript.                                  
 81   c  FUND$This work was supported by Office of Basic Energy Sciences, US    
 81  xc  Department of Energy, under contract DE-AC02-05CH11231.                
 81   c  COMM$All the primary and the secondary references, available within    
 81  2c  the cut-off date, of A = 81 nuclides have been consulted for           
 81  3c  extracting the necessary data. The internal conversion coefficients    
 81  4c  (|a) presented in this evaluation have been calculated using the       
 81  5c  computer code BrIcc (2008Ki07) based on Band-Raman tables of           
 81  6c  conversion coefficients. While extracting the weighted average value   
 81  7c  of a particular spectroscopic quantity from a set of data, care has    
 81  8c  been taken so that the quoted uncertainty in the weighted value does   
 81  9c  not remain lower than the lowest uncertainty associated with the       
 81  ac  individual data points. Rotational band parameters (if given) are      
 81  9c  calculated using the standard energy relation:                         
 81  #c                                                                         
 81  #c  E(J,K)=E{-0}+A[J(J+1)-K{+2}]+B[J(J+1)-K{+2}]{+2}+[A{-2K}+B{-2K}(J(J+1) 
 81  xc  -K{+2})][|d{-K,1/2}(-1){+J+1/2}(J+1/2)]                                
 81  #c                                                                         
 81  #c  where E{-0} and A are given in keV, B and B{-2K} in eV, and the        
 81  xc  decoupling constant {Ba} is dimensionless.                             

