 81CU c  2010Oh02: {+81}Cu nuclide identified in Be({+238}U,F) and              
 81CU2c  Pb({+238}U,F) reactions with a {+238}U{+86+} beam energy of            
 81CU3c  345 MeV/nucleon produced by the cascade operation of the RBIF          
 81CU4c  accelerator complex of the linear accelerator RILAC and four           
 81CU5c  cyclotrons RRC, fRC, IRC and SRC. Identification of {+81}Cu nuclei was 
 81CU6c  made on the basis of magnetic rigidity, time-of-flight and energy loss 
 81CU7c  of the fragments using BigRIPS fragment separator. Experiments         
 81CU8c  performed at RIKEN facility.                                           
 81CU c  Based on A/Q spectrum and Z versus A/Q plot, 36 counts were assigned   
 81CU2c  to {+81}Cu isotope. (Q=charge state)                                   
 81CU c  2014Xu07: {+81}Cu nuclide produced in {+9}Be({+238}U,F)                
 81CU2c  reaction with a {+238}U{+86+} beam of 345 MeV/nucleon produced at the  
 81CU4c  RIKEN accelerator complex. Separation of {+81}Cu nuclei was made on    
 81CU5c  the basis of magnetic rigidity, time-of-flight and energy loss of the  
 81CU6c  fragments (|DE-B|r-tof method) using BigRIPS fragment separator and    
 81CU7c  and ZeroDegree Spectrometer (ZDS) at RIBF-RIKEN facility. Based on A/Q 
 81CU8c  spectrum and Z versus A/Q plot. Measured heavy fragment, |b and |g     
 81CU9c  spectra using wide-range active silicon strip stopper array (WAS3ABi)  
 81CUAc  for beta and ion detection, and EUROBALL-RIKEN Cluster array for |g    
 81CUBc  detection. Decay curves were obtained from time differences between    
 81CUCc  implantation and correlated |b decays                                  
 81CU c  2005Bo19: calculated half-life, |b-delayed neutron emission probability
 81CU d  2000Is13: calculated S(n), S(2n), Q(|b{+-})                            
