 81GA    81ZN B- DECAY (300 MS)        2020PA26,2010PA33,2007IB0125NDS    202501
 81GA  H TYP=FUL$AUT=M. Shamsuzzoha Basunia$CIT=NDS 199, 271 (2025)$            
 81GA2 H CUT=1-Sep-2024$                                                        
 81GA c  Others references: 2007Ve08, 2007VeZZ, 2006VeZZ, 2004Ve14 - from the   
 81GA2c  same research group of 2007Ib01.                                       
 81GA c  2020Pa26: {+81}Zn isotopes were collected on an Al stopper following   
 81GA2c  the separation and acceleration of fission products from |?2000|'C     
 81GA3c  UC{-2}/graphite target by fast neutrons converted from proton pulses,  
 81GA4c  E=1.4-GeV, from the PS-Booster at CERN in intervals of 1.2 s;          
 81GA5c  Detectors: two HPGe, two LaBr{-3}(Ce) detectors, and an NE111A plastic 
 81GA6c  scintillator (3-mm-thick); measured E|g, I|g, |b|g, |g|g coin, |g gated
 81GA7c  time difference spectra; deduced level scheme, half-life of 1st and    
 81GA8c  2nd excited states of {+81}Ga, T{-1/2} and delayed %|b-n branching of  
 81GA9c  {+81}Zn, etc. Contamination of {+81}Rb (T{-1/2}=4.57 h) was present    
 81GAac  but activity was lower during the data taking.                         
 81GA c  2010Pa33: {+81}Zn ions were produced by proton fission of uranium      
 81GA2c  (UC{-x} target) at HRIBF at Oak Ridge National Laboratory using        
 81GA2c  the isotope separation online (ISOL) technique and sent to the         
 81GA3c  Low_energy Radioactive Ion Beam Spectroscopy Station (LeRIBSS) for     
 81GA4c  radiation measurements; Detectors: High purity Ge clovers for |g ray   
 81GA5c  and two plastic |b scintillators for |b ray measurements;              
 81GA6c  measured E|g, I|g, |g|g coin, |b|g coin. Deduced levels, J|p,          
 81GA7c  branching ratios, T{-1/2}.                                             
 81GA c  2007Ve08, 2007Ib01, 2007VeZZ, 2006VeZZ, 2004Ve14:                      
 81GA2c  {+81}Zn source from n-induced fission in |?2000|' C UC{-x}             
 81GA2c  target at the PARRNe ISOL facility; |g rays detected by two coaxial    
 81GA3c  HPGe detectors of the EUROGAM phase I type; |b rays were detected      
 81GA4c  by plastic scintillators. Measured E|g, |g|g coin, |b|g coin, parent   
 81GAxc  T{-1/2}.                                                               
 81GA c                                                                         
 81GA c  In 2004Ve14, a tentative 1621.6|g from 1621.6 keV level was proposed.  
 81GA2c  In 2010Pa33 this |g was not confirmed for {+81}Zn and note that the    
 81GA2c  energy region was contaminated by the 1620.5 {I}-keV line from         
 81GA3c  {+212}Bi decay. Also not reported in 2020Pa26.                         
 81GA c                                                                         
