 81GA c  2016Al10: {+82}Zn produced in the fission of {+238}UC{-x} target of    
 81GA2c  6 g/cm{+2} thickness by a 50 MeV, 10-18 |mA proton beam from the       
 81GA3c  Holifield Radioactive Ion beam facility (HRIBF) at Oak Ridge National  
 81GA4c  Laboratory, followed by a two-step high-resolution mass separation.    
 81GA c  The radioactive ion beam was transmitted to the Low-energy Radioactive 
 81GA2c  Ion Beam Spectroscopy Station (LeRIBSS), then implanted on a moving    
 81GA3c  tape collector (MTC) surrounded by four HPGe detectors for |g rays and 
 81GA4c  two plastic scintillators for |b detection. The counting cycle was     
 81GA5c  four seconds implantation of ion beam on the tape, followed by two     
 81GA6c  seconds of decay measurement, while the ion beam was deflected away.   
 81GA7c  After the decay measurement, the MTC system transported the samples    
 81GA8c  50 cm away from the |g and |b detector system.                         
 81GA c  Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin, half-life of {+82}Zn decay,   
