 81GA c  2012Sa46: Isotopically enriched targets of {+238}UO{-2} and metallic   
 81GA2c  {+238}U with thickness of 400 |mg/cm{+2} and 1000 |mg/cm{+2},          
 81GA3c  respectively. E({+82}Se)=515 MeV beam was delivered by the Tandem-XTU  
 81GA4c  and ALPI superconducting LINAC accelerators at Legnaro National        
 81GA5c  Laboratories (LNL). Nuclide identification through energy loss         
 81GA6c  by PRISMA magnetic spectrometer placed at grazing angle of 64|' with   
 81GA7c  respect to beam direction. Average mass resolution was |DA/A = 1/180.  
 81GA8c  E|g detected by CLARA array composed of 23 Compton-suppressed          
 81GA9c  Ge clover detectors in coincidence with PRISMA spectrometer. Measured  
 81GAac  E|g, |g|g and |g|g|g coincidences through a second experiment at LNL   
 81GAbc  using a {+238}U target of 60 mg/cm{+2} thickness and GASP array.       
 81GA c  2007De37: E({+82}Se)=505 MeV for {+238}U target, 460 MeV for {+192}Os  
 81GA3c  target; isotopically enriched targets; CLARA |g-ray spectrometer (based
 81GA4c  on Compton-suppressed composite EUROBALL Clover detectors) coupled with
 81GA5c  the magnetic spectrometer PRISMA at the Legnaro facility; measured E|g.
 81GA6c  Used thick target and GASP array (40 Compton-suppressed Ge             
 81GA7c  detectors and an inner ball of BGO detectors) to measure |g|g coin.    
