 81AS    81GE B- DECAY (6.4 S)         2022DE07,1981HO24         25NDS    202501
 81AS  H TYP=FUL$AUT=M. Shamsuzzoha Basunia$CIT=NDS 199, 271 (2025)$            
 81AS2 H CUT=1-Sep-2024$                                                        
 81AS c  Others: 1972De43, 1980HoZN, 1981Al20, 1981ZeZY, 1990Ru05.              
 81AS c  2022De07: {+81}Ge was obtained at the IGISOL facility of the University
 81AS2c  of Jyvaskyla exposing {+232}Th target (15 mg/cm{+2}) with proton beam, 
 81AS3c  E=35-MeV. {+81}Ge ions were selected in the first trap (also called    
 81AS4c  purification trap). Only J{+|p}=9/2{++} g.s. of {+81}Ge was observed   
 81AS5c  - confirmed by a tof Ion-Cyclotron-Resonance measurement in a second   
 81AS6c  measurement trap. Direct population of J{+|p}=1/2{++} isomeric state   
 81AS7c  was negligible. Two coaxial detectors GC7020, two EUROGAM-2-like CLOVER
 81AS8c  detectors, a BEGe2020 detector with a Be entrance window. Measured E|g,
 81AS9c  I|g, |g-|g coin; deduce level scheme, |b feeding.                      
 81AS c  Source: from mass-separated fission products.                          
 81AS c  1981Ho24, 1980HoZN: single |g and |g|g-coin measured with              
 81AS2c  Ge(Li); x-ray detector for low energy |g search (E|g|>15 keV);         
 81AS3c  Si(Li) detector for simultaneous measurement of ce and |g              
 81AS4c  spectra (for |a(K)exp determination).                                  
 81AS c  In 1980HoZN (lab report of 1981Ho24), E|g, I|g and |g|g coin data      
 81AS2c  are tabulated without differentiation between their {+81}Ge            
 81ASxc  parentages.                                                            
 81AS c  From analysis of {+81}Ga decay and |b|g-coin measurements, it is       
 81AS2c  evident that there are two |b{+-} decaying isomers of {+81}Ge; but, in 
 81AS3c  a multispectrum analysis of mass number 81, 1981Ho24 were unable       
 81AS4c  to differentiate between their half-lives. Hence, 1981Ho24             
 81AS5c  conclude that there exist two isomers of {+81}Ge which possess similar 
 81AS6c  T{-1/2} values. Presumably other authors also report T{-1/2}           
 81AS8c  relevant to a mixture of these isomers.                                
 81AS c  1981Ho24 propose tentative decay schemes for the two isomers,          
 81AS2c  consistent with |g|g and |b|g coin data and supported by arguments     
 81AS3c  based on the large spin differences of the decaying                    
 81AS4c  isomers and on analogies with {+83}Se decay. However, J|p based on the 
 81AS5c  resulting log| {Ift} values and observed |g deexcitation patterns      
 81AS6c  are in conflict with L(t,|a) for the 758 and 1613 levels unless        
 81AS7c  separate levels with almost identical energies are assumed to be       
 81AS8c  excited in |b{+-} decay and in (t,|a).                                 
 81AS cB           From |g gated |b{+-} endpoint measurements, 1981Al20         
 81AS2cB determine Q(|b) values of 6220 {I130} and 6930 {I280} for g.s. and     
 81AS3cB isomeric state |b{+-} decay, respectively. These imply E(isomeric      
 81AS4cB state, {+81}Ge)=710 {I310}.                                            
 81AS cB           Measured average E|b=1580 {I150} (1990Ru05).                 
 81AS cG           Measured average E|g=2000 {I222} (1990Ru05).                 
