 81SE c  {U Other Reactions:}                                                   
 81SE c  {+2}H({+80}Se,p|g), E({+80}Se)|?320 MeV (2007Ci05); investigated       
 81SE2c  feasibility of measuring |g-rays in coincidence with (d,p) reaction    
 81SE3c  protons in inverse kinematics using Cd{-2} targets; observed           
 81SE4c  765|g-468|g cascade and 1233|g from 1233 level.                        
 81SE c  2015Al19: Isotopic yield cross section |s({+81}Se)=0.011 mb {I3}, in   
 81SE2c  spallation of {+136}Xe-induced reactions on deuterium at 500           
 81SE3c  MeV/nucleon.                                                           
 81SE cG E,RI      From {+80}Se(n,|g) E=thermal, except as noted                
 81SE cG E(D),RI(DG)$From {+81}As |b{+-} decay.                                 
 81SE cG E(CE),RI(E)$From ({+18}O,x|g)                                          
 81SE cG E(F)      Assumed to be of M1 (dipole) transition (by authors          
 81SE2cG ({+18}O,x|g)), based on the 1079|g crossover transition.               
 81SE cL E         From a least-squares fit to E|g if |DE<1 keV; from (p,d) if  
 81SE2cL |DE=25 keV; from (pol d,p) otherwise. Based on a comparison with       
 81SE3cL E(level) derived from E|g data for E(level)<3550, E(level) data from   
 81SE4cL 1978Mo12 and 1960Ca16 in (d,p) are reliable to better than 6 keV       
 81SE5cL (typically 0-2 keV), with the exception of the 635 level (which is 11  
 81SE6cL keV high). For E(level)>1400, E(level) values from (p,d) are 10-30 keV 
 81SE7cL higher than those from (d,p). The evaluator, therefore, adopts E(level)
 81SE8cL from (d,p) in preference to E(level) from (p,d).                       
 81SE cL E(A)      Estimated |DE|?6 keV from level energy deviations of (d,p)   
 81SE2cL dataset from adopted values by more than 6 keV.                        
 81SE cL J         From (pol d,p), unless noted otherwise. From DWBA analysis of
 81SE2cL angular distribution and vector analyzing power (1978Mo12).            
 81SE cL J(B)      L(p,d)=(2+3) for 2763 {I25} state. Evaluator assumes this to 
 81SE2cL be 2770+2774 doublet, in which case the L=(2) component would          
 81SE3cL correspond to the 2774 level, leaving the L=(3) component to           
 81SE4cL correspond to the 2770 level, thus favoring J|p=5/2-,7/2- for it.      
 81SE cL J(D)      L(p,d)=(3+4) for 2893 {I25} state. Evaluator assumes this to 
 81SE2cL be 2891+2935 doublet, in which case the L=(3) component would          
 81SE3cL correspond to the 2935 level leaving the L=(4) component to            
 81SE4cL correspond to the 2891 level, favoring J|p=7/2+,9/2+ for this level.   
 81SE cL J(E)      L(p,d)=(3+4) for 2985 {I25} state. Evaluator assumes this to 
 81SE2cL be a doublet, in which case the L=(3) component could                  
 81SE3cL correspond to the 2965 level leaving the L=(4) component to            
 81SE4cL correspond to an E|?2986 level and favoring J|p=7/2+,9/2+ for this     
 81SE5cL level. The L(d,p)=(0) state at E=2986 is then presumed to be a         
 81SE6cL different level.                                                       
 81SE cL J(F)       Based on the assumption (by authors in 2009Po04             
 81SE2cL ({+18}O,x|g)) that in yrast decays spin values increase with excitation
 81SE3cL  energy. See the dataset for other assumptions.                        
