 81SE3c  known primary |g, E|g alone for several additional secondary           
 81SE4c  transitions; same as 2003ChZS.                                         
 81SE#c  1981En07: natural target, reported three primary |g-rays.              
 81SE#c  1970Ba54: 95.7% {+80}Se target, four primary and three secondary       
 81SE6c  |g-rays reported.                                                      
 81SE c  |s{-|g}=0.593 b {I46} {+81}Se{+m+g} (2018MuZY, 2008Na01)               
 81SE c  S(n)=6101.1 {I6} measured by 1981En07 cf. 6700.8 {I3} from 2021Wa16.   
 81SE cG           No capture state to g.s. transition was found (I|g<0.2%).    
 81SE cG           The relatively strong 521|g branch deexciting the 624 level  
 81SE2cG in {+81}As |b{+-} decay is not reported in (n,|g); however, it would   
 81SE3cG probably have been masked in (n,|g) by a {+77}Se impurity |g (see      
 81SExcG 1974Ch11).                                                             
 81SE cG E         From 1971Ra07, except as noted. Several otherwise unknown    
 81SE2cG transitions listed in 2007ChZX, 'Budapest' data are not included       
 81SE3cG here because it is unclear whether these were actually observed or     
 81SE4cG merely expected (no I|g reported).                                     
