 81SE2cG of this |g.                                                            
 81SE cG RI        Photons per 100 captures in {+80}Se from 1971Ra07, except as 
 81SE2cG noted. Authors' uncertainties in relative I|g are shown;               
 81SE3cG the additional uncertainty in absolute I|g is |?10% for E|g|<2 MeV,    
 81SE4cG 15% for E|g>2 MeV noted in 1971Ra07 - the evaluator assigns 15% for    
 81SE5cG all. Except for the 468|g and 4976|g, 'Budapest' data from 2007ChZX    
 81SE5cG (which supersedes 2003ChZS) is in poor agreement.                      
 81SE cG RI(B)     I|g=6.2 {I5} for doublet. Assuming I(388|g)/I(491|g)=0.101   
 81SE2cG {I12} for 491 level branching (from |b{+-} decay), I|g=6.6 {I9} for    
 81SE3cG the 491 to g.s. component of 491|g in (n,|g), leaving I|g=-0.4 {I10}   
 81SE4cG for the 1725 to 1233 component. The evaluator,                         
 81SE5cG therefore, assigns the entire doublet I|g to the former transition and 
 81SE6cG an upper limit of 0.6 to the latter. Placement of latter component is, 
 81SE7cG consequently, shown as tentative.                                      
 81SE cG RI(D)     I|g=0.36 {I4} for doublet. Assuming I(938|g)/I(1406|g)=0.33  
 81SE2cG {I6} for 1407-level branching (from |b{+-} decay), I|g=0.43 {I10} for  
 81SE3cG 1407 to 468 transition in (n,|g), leaving I|g=-0.07 {I11} for 1828 to  
 81SE4cG 889 component. Evaluator, therefore assigns the entire doublet I|g to  
 81SE5cG the former transition and an upper limit of 0.04 to the latter.        
 81SE cL E         From a least-squares fit to E|g, excluding E|g for all       
 81SE2cL multiply-placed lines.                                                 
 81SE cL J         From Adopted Levels.                                         
 81SE cL E(E)      1971Ra07 show no |g deexciting this level; however, the      
 81SE2cL unplaced 3056.5|g has plausible E|g and I|g for a 3526 to 468 level    
 81SE3cL transition.                                                            
 81SE cL J(F)$J|p based on s-wave thermal neutron capture by J|p=0+ target.     
 81SE cL T(G)      Since 468|g and 491|g are each coin with |g rays feeding the 
 81SE2cL 468 and 491 levels when the coin resolving time is 40 ns, T{-1/2} for  
 81SE3cL either level cannot be significantly greater than 40 ns.               
 81SE  N 1.00      15                                                           
 81SE cN NR        Absolute intensity (intensity/100 neutron captures by        
 81SE2cN {+80}Se) measured by 1971Ra07. Intensities calibrated relative to      
 81SE3cN I(479|g) in boron(n,|g) (for low E|g) and I(7367.7|g) in Pb(n,|g) (for 
 81SE4cN high E|g); uncertainty |?10% for E|g|<2000, 15% for E|g>2000. Absolute 
 81SE5cN intensity data from 'Budapest data' in 2007ChZX are in satisfactory    
 81SE6cN agreement for the 468|g and 4976|g, but are typically high by factors  
 81SE7cN of 2 to 16 for the other lines common to both studies.                 
