 81BR2 H CUT=1-Sep-2024$                                                        
 81BR c  E=400 keV to 1900 keV. 49.5% {+81}Br target; measured E|g, I|g.        
 81BR c  Level scheme constructed by authors of 1971Ba78 based on |g energy and 
 81BR2c  summing, aided by knowledge of level energies from |b{+-} decay        
 81BR3c  (1969Zo06) and Coulomb excitation.                                     
 81BR cG E         |DE not stated by authors in 1971Ba78.                       
 81BR cG E(D)      Presence in this reaction is uncertain due to interference   
 81BR2cG from a relatively intense {+79}Br line.                                
 81BR cG E(A),RI(A)$I|g normalized so that I(276.4|g)=100 for E(n)=1900 keV.    
 81BR2cG Uncertain whether |g is due to {+81}Br or {+79}Br.                     
 81BR cG E(E),RI(E)$In (p,|g) reaction, a 789.6|g is assigned to deexcite a     
 81BR2cG 1327 keV level; however, this 789.9|g must have a different origin     
 81BR3cG because 1971Ba78 observe it for E(n)|>900.                             
 81BR cG RI        % photon branching from each level measured at 85|'. Authors 
 81BR2cG assume that corrections for angular correlation effects or internal    
 81BR3cG conversion will be small, so do not include them. Quoted uncertainty is
 81BR4cG 10% for E|g<1000, 25% for E|g|>1000; it is not clear whether this is   
 81BR5cG absolute or fractional uncertainty in branching (the latter has been   
 81BR6cG assumed here). If branching is not shown, transition is either         
 81BR7cG very weak or unresolved from another line.                             
 81BR cL E         From 1971Ba78; |DE<1 keV for E<1000, <2 keV otherwise noted  
 81BR2cL authors in the text. |DE|g not listed by authors.                      
 81BR cL E(B)      Level should be considered as tentative because the          
 81BR2cL transitions involved are weak or can also be placed                    
 81BR3cL elsewhere in {+79}Br or {+81}Br level schemes.                         
 81BR cL E(G)      Deexcitation of this 1266 level differs significantly from   
 81BR2cL that reported in (|a,p2n|g) for a (9/2)- level at the same energy.     
 81BR3cL The 430|g is present in both reactions, but the 500|g and 1266|g are   
 81BR4cL absent in (|a,p2n|g), whereas the strongest branch in (|a,p2n|g)       
 81BR5cL (E|g=990.4) does not appear in the level scheme of 1971Ba78. The       
 81BR6cL unplaced 992|g could perhaps correspond to the 990|g of (|a,p2n|g) and 
 81BR7cL the multiply placed 1266|g may be misplaced here, but the absence in   
 81BR8cL (|a,p2n|g) of the 500|g and the level it feeds strongly suggests that  
 81BR9cL different levels are excited in these two reactions.                   
