 81KR cL T(L)$2.13|*10{+5} y {I+16-26} from 1964Ea05 (Authors also reported     
 81KR2cL uncertainty as +0.016-0.26 - appears to be a misprint). In 1964Ea05,   
 81KR3cL |w{-K}(Br)=0.5775 and |eK=0.8417 (from total-to-K-capture ratio of     
 81KR4cL 1.188 {I+85-16}) were used. Note that for efficiency calibration {+88}Y
 81KR5cL was used with |w{-K}(Sr)=0.653 [in their Ref. 14 (1960Ha39)] and       
 81KR6cL |eK=0.8818 (from total-to-K-capture ratio of 1.134). Current values of 
 81KR7cL |eK remain almost the same (0.8473 and |?0.87, respectively), however, 
 81KR8cL different |w{-K} value exits in the literature [|w{-K}(Br)=0.586 {I9} -
 81KR9cL average of expt. value (1994Hu23 p.351), 0.598 (1994Hu23), 0.618       
 81KRacL (1979Kr22), 0.628 (listed from literature in 1994Hu23 p.351)].         
 81KRbcL Consideration of any of these |w{-K}(Br) values would yield a higher   
 81KRccL half-life compared to the reported one by the same factor. For example,
 81KRdcL in the previous evaluations (2008Ba34, 1996Ba89,1993Ba30) adjusted     
 81KRecL value of T{-1/2}=2.29 |* 10{+5} y {I11} was recommended, assuming      
 81KRfcL |w{-K}(Br)=0.618 {I19} and |eK=0.8473. The uncertainty was the 5% as   
 81KRgcL mentioned in 1964Ea05 (estimated uncertainty from six measurements).   
 81KRhcL Note that another 5.7% [|w{-K}(Sr)0.69 (1994Hu23)/0.653] decrease can  
 81KRicL be expected if one considers the adjustment of efficiency calibration  
 81KRjcL for the {+88}Y source. Here, the evaluator reports the same T{-1/2}    
 81KRkcL value of 1964Ea05, based on the close experimental value of            
 81KRlcL |w{-K}(Br)=0.586 {I9} (1994Hu23) and 0.5775, used in 1964Ea05. Other:  
 81KRmcL 2.1|*10{+5} y {I5} (1950Re54).                                         
