 81RB  H TYP=FUL$AUT=M. Shamsuzzoha Basunia$CIT=NDS 199, 271 (2025)$            
 81RB2 H CUT=1-Sep-2024$                                                        
 81RB dG $Transition strength is calculated by Java-RULER (version 19-Aug-2022) 
 81RB c  {U Other Reactions:}                                                   
 81RB c  Measured yields of {+81}Rb for 1000 stopped antiproton on {+95}Mo and  
 81RB2c  {+98}Mo: 35 {I7} and 22 {I6}, respectively. The targets were irradiated
 81RB3c  at LEAR, CERN with an average proton rate of 10{+4} per sec for        
 81RB4c  about six hours. Identified residual {+81}Rb by |g-spectroscopy        
 81RB5c  (1986Mo20).                                                            
 81RB c  2015Al19: Isotopic yield cross section |s({+81}Rb)=0.780 mb {I75}, in  
 81RB2c  spallation of {+136}Xe-induced reactions on deuterium at 500           
 81RB3c  MeV/nucleon.                                                           
 81RB  Q -3929     6 11353   5 4852    5 -4647   6     2021WA16                 
 81RB cQ $S(2n)=20797 {I5}, S(2p)=13967 {I5} (2021Wa16)                         
 81RB cG E(J)$Poor fit; uncertainty multiplied by a factor in the fitting       
 81RB cG           For all but 10 transitions observed in in-beam studies, |DE  
 81RB2cG is unstated by authors.                                                
 81RB cG E,RI      From {+81}Sr |e decay, except as noted.                      
 81RB cG E(EK),RI(CK)$From {+79}Br(|a,2n|g), {+68}Zn({+16}O,p2n|g). For I|g     
 81RB2cG uncertainty 10%-50% in {+79}Br(|a,2n|g).                               
 81RB cG E(F)      From {+53}Cr({+31}P,2pn|g).                                  
 81RB cG E(I)      From {+68}Zn({+19}F,|a2n|g).                                 
 81RB cG E(H)      Reported only in preliminary results from                    
 81RB2cG {+53}Cr({+31}P,2pn|g); consequently, evaluator shows it here as        
 81RBxcG tentative.                                                             
 81RB cG E(A)      347.3|g deexcites this level in (|a,2n|g), based on |g|g coin
 81RB2cG data; a 347.8|g deexcites the 923 level in {+81}Sr |e decay, but the   
 81RB3cG stronger 923|g deexciting that level is absent in in-beam reaction     
 81RB4cG studies. The evaluator, therefore, assumes that different 347|g        
 81RB5cG lines are observed in the two reactions.                               
 81RB cG E(B)      301.30|g deexcites this level in |e decay; 300.7|g deexcites 
 81RB2cG 913 level in in-beam studies, based on |g|g-coin information. Evaluator
 81RB3cG presumes that these are different |g rays since the 759|g, which also  
 81RB4cG deexcites the 913 level in in-beam studies, is absent in |e decay.     
 81RB cG E(D)      This |g from {+81}Sr |e decay presumably differs from the    
 81RB2cG 1211|g deexciting the 1920-keV level in (|a,2n|g) (placement based on  
 81RB3cG |g|g-coin data) since the 932|g, which also deexcites that             
 81RB4cG level in (|a,2n|g), is absent in Rb |e decay.                          
 81RB cG RI(G)     Based on transition line width in level scheme drawing for   
 81RB2cG {+68}Zn({+19}F,|a2n|g), {+79}Br(|a,2n|g) E=27 MeV (fig. 4 of 1994Do18),
 81RB2cG this |g is the strongest among several deexciting its parent level.    
 81RB cG M         The transitions designated as "Q", here or in comments, are  
 81RB2cG stretched transitions.                                                 
 81RB cL           Band structure is from 1994Do18 with minor band extensions   
 81RB2cL from 1993LiZR (the structure deduced in 1989Ta09 is basically          
 81RB3cL consistent, but much less extensive). 1994Do18 report four more bands  
 81RB4cL than 1993LiZR, but 1993LiZR extend slightly the bands common to both   
 81RB5cL studies. There are, however, several significant inconsistencies       
 81RB6cL between the schemes of 1993LiZR and 1994Do18. Most involve the         
 81RB7cL 3-quasiparticle structure and its interconnection with the lowest |p=- 
 81RB8cL and |p=+ bands; 1994Do18 report 13 interconnecting transitions,        
 81RB9cL 1993LiZR report 9, but only 2 transitions are common to both studies.  
 81RBAcL Another difference concerns the parity of the 3056 level (|p=- in      
 81RBBcL 1994Do18, |p=+ in 1993LiZR and 1989Ta09); see comment on J|p for 3056  
 81RBCcL level. The published study of 1994Do18 has the better statistical      
 81RBDcL accuracy, the unpublished study of 1993LiZR has the potential for      
 81RBEcL populating bands to higher spin. Therefore, the evaluator tentatively  
 81RBFcL adopts band extensions indicated in 1993LiZR, but does not adopt any   
 81RBGcL other structure from 1993LiZR unless it has been confirmed in 1994Do18.
 81RBHcL The reader is referred to the {+53}Cr({+31}P,2pn|g) data               
 81RBIcL set for details of 1993LiZR data not adopted here.                     
 81RB cL E         Level energies quoted to the nearest keV are from (|a,p)     
 81RB2cL and/or ({+3}He,d), if |g deexcitation has not been observed; |DE is    
 81RB3cL unstated in both reactions, but probably does not exceed |?35 keV (see 
 81RB4cL comments in (|a,p) and ({+3}He,d) data sets). The other values         
 81RB5cL are from a least-squares fit to E|g, omitting 978.7|g,                 
 81RB6cL 1252.8|g, 1382.4|g and 1554.1|g (each of which is at least 3|s from    
 81RB7cL least-squares adjusted value) and arbitrarily assigning |DE=1 keV      
 81RB8cL to E|g values whose uncertainties are unknown.                         
 81RB cL J         Values which are assigned without comment are based on       
 81RB2cL band structure deduced in {+68}Zn({+19}F,|a2n|g) and/or                
 81RB3cL {+53}Cr({+31}P,2pn|g), combined with |g multipolarity information      
 81RB4cL (from unenumerated DCO ratios in {+53}Cr({+31}P,2pn|g), or mostly      
 81RB4cL unstated |g(|q) and |g asymmetry ratio data from                       
 81RBxcL {+68}Zn({+19}F,|a2n|g)).                                               
 81RB cL J(I)      |p is adopted from {+68}Zn({+19}F,|a2n|g). Opposite |p was   
 81RB2cL suggested in {+53}Cr({+31}P,2pn|g) and {+55}Mn({+29}Si,2pn|g), neither 
 81RB3cL of which reported the 761.4|g which feeds the (15/2-) 2294 level of the
 81RB4cL near-yrast |p=-, |a=-1/2 band in {+68}Zn({+19}F,|a2n|g) (that |g could 
 81RB5cL plausibly have been masked by the strong 759.7|g from the 9/2- member  
 81RB6cL of the |p=-, |a=+1/2 near-yrast band). J=19/2 is based on a definite D 
 81RB7cL component in the 1472|g feeding the 17/2+ member of the yrast band and 
 81RB8cL a (Q) 901|g from the (23/2-) 3957 level (which also feeds the 21/2-    
 81RB9cL and 19/2- members of the 3-quasiparticle band).                        
 81RB cL T         From RDM in {+65}Cu({+19}F,p2n|g) if E<2610, and from DSA in 
 81RB2cL {+55}Mn({+29}Si,2pn|g) if E|>2610, except as noted.                    
