 81RB2    56FE(28SI,3PG)                                                        
 81RB  H TYP=FUL$AUT=M. Shamsuzzoha Basunia$CIT=NDS 199, 271 (2025)$            
 81RB2 H CUT=1-Sep-2024$                                                        
 81RB c  {U{+55}Mn({+29}Si,2pn|g)}:                                             
 81RB c  1989Ta09: E({+29}Si)=95.2 MeV, Compton-suppressed Ge detectors at 23|' 
 81RB2c  and 100|', Ge(Li) detector at -100|'; measured E|g, T{-1/2} from DSA,  
 81RB3c  |g|g coin, directional correlation of oriented nuclei ratios [R(DCO);  
 81RB4c  |q=23|', 100|'].                                                       
 81RB c  {U{+56}Fe({+28}Si,3p|g)}:                                              
 81RB c  1982Th03: E({+28}Si)=80-99 MeV, 99.8% {+56}Fe target,                  
 81RB2c  Ge(Li) with FWHM=1.97 keV at 1.33 MeV;                                 
 81RB3c  measured E|g, I|g, |g|g coin (FWHM 15 ns), |g(|q) for                  
 81RB4c  |q=0|', 30|', 45|', 60|', 90|', excit (5-MeV steps).                   
 81RB cG           R(DCO) values listed in the comments are from 1989Ta09.      
 81RB cG E         From 1989Ta09; |DE not stated by authors.                    
 81RB cG E(E)      A second 301|g, a 429|g and a 958|g appear to be coincident  
 81RB2cG with each other, forming a cascade of unknown sequence feeding the     
 81RB3cG 1738 (13/2-) level.                                                    
 81RB cG M         From 1989Ta09, based on DCO ratios. R(DCO)|?1 is expected    
 81RB2cG for unmixed |DJ=2 transitions. R(DCO) can vary from |?0 to |?2         
 81RB3cG for |DJ=1 transitions, but systematics indicate R(DCO)|?0.5 for        
 81RB4cG most M1(+E2) transitions in yrast cascades.                            
 81RB cG M(D)      1989Ta09 tentatively assign |DJ=2, assuming R(DCO) to be low 
 81RB2cG due to strong Doppler shifting and broadening of the 1493|g in the     
 81RB3cG 23|' spectrum.                                                         
 81RB cL           Level scheme is from 1989Ta09, based on mult., I|g, extensive
 81RB2cL |g|g-coin data and (HI,xn|g) reaction systematics. Detailed |g|g-coin  
 81RB3cL information is not given in 1989Ta09. A number of non-yrast states     
 81RB4cL were also excited in 1989Ta09, but no specific information was given.  
 81RB cL E         From a least-squares fit to E|g, allowing equal weights      
 81RB2cL for all E|g.                                                           
 81RB cL E(F),J(F) See comment on 1057|g; E(level)=4820 or 3664, J|p=27/2+ or   
 81RB2cL 23/2+, respectively, depending on placement of 1057|g. The adopted     
 81RB2cL value corresponds to the second alternative.                           
 81RB cG E(F)      A Doppler broadened 1057|g is coincident with 622|g, 874|g   
 81RB2cG and 1024|g, representing a transition to either the 3763 (25/2+) level 
 81RB3cG or the 2607 (21/2+) level (1989Ta09); the latter option has, in fact,  
 81RB4cG been established in a subsequent ({+19}F,|a2n|g) study.                
 81RB cL J         From 1989Ta09, based on R(DCO) values and reaction           
 81RB2cL systematics, except as noted.                                          
 81RB cL T         From DSAM (1989Ta09), corrected for side-feeding, except     
 81RB2cL as noted.                                                              
