 81RB cL           Decay schemes of 1973Br32 and 1981FrZY are based on Ritz     
 81RB2cL combination principle, intensity balances, and coincidence             
 81RB3cL measurements. The 1980Ho28 scheme is based only on the                 
 81RB4cL Ritz principle and intensity balances. Different authors               
 81RB5cL propose significantly different decay schemes. The adopted scheme is   
 81RB6cL essentially that of 1980Ho28 with the addition of levels at 1061 keV   
 81RB7cL and 1218 keV (proposed in 1981FrZY) and the |g|g-coin data from        
 81RB8cL 1973Br32 and 1981FrZY. Levels at 497, 819, 866, 1344 and               
 81RB9cL 1600, proposed in 1973Br32, are not adopted because |g rays deexciting 
 81RBAcL them are either placed differently or are unobserved by 1980Ho28 or    
 81RBBcL 1981FrZY.                                                              
 81RB cL E         From a least-squares fit to E|g, omitting 978.66, 1252.82 and
 81RB2cL 1554.15 from 1553.7 keV level; 1382.44 from 1381.9 keV level. Without  
 81RB3cL and with considerations |h{+2}=3.4 and 1.8, respectively, cf.          
 81RB4cL |h{+2}{-crit}=1.5.                                                     
