 81RB cL J,T       From Adopted Levels.                                         
 81RB cG E,RI      From 1980Ho28, if not noted otherwise. I|g data from 1980Ho28
 81RB2cG and 1973Br32 are in reasonable agreement, whereas data from 1981FrZY   
 81RB3cG frequently disagree significantly with those from 1980Ho28. Fourteen   
 81RB4cG weaker |g rays (E|g=98 {I1}, 172.0 {I5}, 177.6 {I5}, 237.5             
 81RB5cG {I10}, 314 {I1}, 319 {I1}, 496.5 {I10}, 517 {I1}, 545.2 {I5}, 586.2    
 81RB6cG {I10}, 819.2 {I10}, 1034.8 {I8}, 1344 {I1}, 1620 {I2}) reported in     
 81RB7cG 1973Br32 are absent in the higher resolution and statistically         
 81RB8cG superior spectra of 1980Ho28 and consequently omitted here; so         
 81RB9cG is E|g=97.6 {I5} from 1982Th03. E|g=507.0, 516.4, 543.3, 589.1, 975.1? 
 81RBacG from 1981FrZY are also absent in 1980Ho28; the 507|g is retained here  
 81RBbcG because it is observable only in coin spectra (unmeasured by           
 81RBccG 1980Ho28), the others are omitted because they are only tentatively    
 81RBdcG assigned to {+81}Rb or are presumed by 1981FrZY to be identical to |g  
 81RBfcG rays from 1973Br32 which are not adopted here.                         
 81RB cG E(A)      E|g at least 3|s from a least-squares adjusted value; datum  
 81RB2cG omitted from least-squares level energy adjustment. |g could be        
 81RB3cG complex or misplaced.                                                  
 81RB cG E(D),RI(D)$From 1981FrZY; not reported in 1980Ho28. Observed only in   
 81RB2cG |g|g coin spectra owing to proximity of strong |g{+|+} peak.           
 81RB cG E(G)      A 487|g placed from a 487 level in 1980Ho28 (as in           
 81RB2cG (|a,2n|g)) is placed from a 1061 level in 1981FrZY based on observed   
 81RB3cG coincidence with 421|g and 574|g, both of which deexcite the 574       
 81RB4cG level. Since several |g rays can be placed feeding a 487 level, and    
 81RB5cG the 1061 level deexcites to a level absent in (|a,2n|g), the evaluator 
 81RB6cG retains both 487 and 1061 levels, assuming the 487|g to be a doublet   
 81RB7cG in {+81}Sr |e decay. The quoted E|g applies to that doublet. Intensity 
 81RB8cG balance at the 486 level requires I(486|g)|>5.9 {I4} from that level,  
 81RB9cG whereas I|g(doublet)=7.3 {I5}. Thus, I(486|g) from 486 level could     
 81RBacG range from 5.5 to 7.8 so the evaluator assigns 6.7 {I11}, leaving 0.6  
 81RBbcG {I12} for I(486|g) from the 1061 level.                                
 81RB cE           The decay scheme is incomplete and the normalization to be   
 81RB2cE considered as approximate.                                             
 81RB cE TI        From total transition intensity balance, I|g(1+|a), at each  
 81RB2cE level.                                                                 
