 81RB c  {+79}Br(|a,2n|g): E|a=27 MeV; natural Br and 98.6% {+79}Br targets;    
 81RB2c  two GeLi detectors at 90|', LEP detector, HPGe detector;               
 81RB3c  measured E|g, |g|g coin, |g(|q).                                       
 81RB c  {+68}Zn({+19}F,|a2n|g): E({+19}F)=72 MeV; thin and Bi-backed 99%       
 81RB2c  {+68}Zn targets, NORDBALL detector array (18 or 19 Compton-suppressed  
 81RB3c  HPGe detectors with 10 or 39 BaF{-2}-detector multiplicity filter),    
 81RB4c  Compton-suppressed low-energy photon spectrometer; measured E|g, |g    
 81RB5c  asymmetry ratios, |g|g coin, T{-1/2}.                                  
 81RB cG E         Authors state |DE for only the ten lines indicated.          
 81RB cG RI        Authors do not report intensities; however, in some cases,   
 81RB2cG it is clear from the level scheme drawing in fig. 4 of 1994Do18        
 81RB3cG which |g-ray among several deexciting a given level is most intense,   
 81RB4cG and such cases are noted here.                                         
 81RB cG M         From indicated |g(|q) in (|a,2n|g) and/or asymmetry ratio    
 81RB2cG [I|g(37|' + 143|')/I|g(79|' + 101|')] in ({+19}F,|a2n|g).              
 81RB3cG Here, the "asymmetry ratio" is equivalent to a DCO ratio summed over   
 81RB4cG all different detector plane angles (1994Do18).                        
 81RB cG M(A)$ A{-2}, A{-4} are unusually large and imply a significantly mixed 
 81RB2cG |DJ=1 transition, whereas an E1 transition is implied by the level     
 81RB3cG scheme. The asymmetry ratio is not inconsistent with a pure D          
 81RB4cG transition. Possibly the singles spectra from which |g(|q) was         
 81RB5cG determined including a contaminant line.                               
 81RB cG RI(G)     Based on transition line width in level scheme drawing       
 81RB2cG in fig. 4 of 1994Do18, this |g is the strongest among several          
 81RB3cG deexciting its parent level.                                           
