 81SR cL E(J),J(J)$ Assuming the 1288|g placement given in ({+30}Si,|a2pn|g) and
 81SR2cL ({+31}P,p2n|g); in ({+19}F,2pn|g), the 1288|g was placed between the   
 81SR3cL 1381 and 1197 cascading gammas, thereby altering the energy for all    
 81SR4cL J|>31/2 members of the 1/2[431] |a=-1/2 band. The level is shown       
 81SR5cL here as tentative because the members of the 1540.0|g-1470.3|g-1380.6|g
 81SR6cL cascade, placed above the 27/2+ 5083 level in ({+31}P,p2n|g) and also  
 81SR7cL present in ({+30}Si,|a2pn|g), could not be fitted into a               
 81SR8cL self-consistent level scheme in the ({+30}Si,|a2pn|g) study.           
 81SR CL BAND(Q)$|a=-1/2, (|n 5/2[422])(|p g{-9/2}){+2} band. Yrast following   
 81SR2cL crossing of 1-quasineutron band at ~h|w|?0.50 MeV.                     
 81SR CL BAND(U)$Possible |p=-, |a=-1/2, 5-quasiparticle band. Feeds into |n    
 81SR2cL 5/2[303] |a=-1/2 band. No signature partner is observed. Postulated to 
 81SR3cL contain the simultaneous alignment of a pair of quasineutrons and a    
 81SR4cL pair of quasiprotons (1996Sm07), resulting in increased deformation.   
