 81SR    53CR(31P,P2NG)                1993LIZX                  25NDS    202501
 81SR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=M. Shamsuzzoha Basunia$CIT=NDS 199, 271 (2025)$            
 81SR2 H CUT=1-Sep-2024$                                                        
 81SR c  1993LiZX: E=95 MeV; Tessa3 array (16 BGO suppressed Ge detectors       
 81SR2c  with 50-element inner BGO ball for |g sum-energy and multiplicity      
 81SR3c  measurements); measured E|g, |g|g coin, |g|g|g coin.                   
 81SR c  It should be noted that 1993LiZX constitutes a preliminary report of   
 81SR2c  data from this reaction.                                               
 81SR cG E(A)      Placed by 1993LiZX from a 11068-keV level (nominated to be   
 81SR2cG the 45/2+ member of the 5/2[542] band); however, that placement is     
 81SR3cG rejected in different reaction studies which extend the band to        
 81SR3cG which 1993LiZX assigned this level.                                    
 81SR cG E(B)      See comment on level deexcited by this |g.                   
 81SR cG E(F)      Placed elsewhere (viz., from 43/2 member of same band) in    
 81SR2cG Adopted Levels, Gammas                                                 
 81SR cG E(H)      This transition would be expected to appear in (|a,xn|g)     
 81SR2cG and/or other (HI,xn|g) studies, but it does not; this casts doubt      
 81SR3cG on the present placement, especially so since the present level scheme 
 81SR4cG is preliminary. Consequently, it is not included in Adopted Gammas.    
 81SR cL E         From a least-squares fit to E|g, allowing equal weight       
 81SR2cL for all gammas.                                                        
 81SR cL J         Values proposed by authors in preliminary level scheme;      
 81SR2cL basis for assignments not stated. Values are consistent with adopted   
 81SR3cL values apart from the addition of parentheses in Adopted Levels for    
 81SR4cL many levels.                                                           
 81SR cL E(B)      Adopted energy for this band member differs from that shown  
 81SR2cL here because the 1016|g, placed by 1993LiZX as the 21/2 to 17/2        
 81SR3cL transition, was shown in a subsequent ({+30}Si,|a2pn|g) reaction study 
 81SR4cL to be absent from this band's |g cascade. With the omission of the     
 81SR5cL 1016|g, the 25/2 to 21/2 transition of 1993LiZX becomes the 21/2 to    
 81SR6cL 17/2 transition in Adopted Levels, Gammas, etc., leading to adopted    
 81SR7cL energies of 3800, 4934, 6068 keV for the 21/2, 25/2, 29/2 band members,
 81SR8cL and eliminating the 33/2 member proposed by 1993LiZX. The 25/2 and 29/2
 81SR9cL members have not been independently observed, so should be considered  
 81SRAcL tentative, at best.                                                    
 81SR cL E(D)      The members of the 1540.0|g-1470.3|g-1380.6|g cascade, placed
 81SR2cL above the 27/2+ 5083 level in 1993LiZX, have also been reported in a   
 81SR3cL ({+30}Si,|a2pn|g) study but, in that study, they could not be fitted   
 81SR4cL into a self-consistent level scheme. The evaluator, therefore,         
 81SR5cL considers the levels defined by those transitions in the present       
 81SR6cL reaction to be uncertain.                                              
 81SR cL E(E)      Not adopted; the 1578|g placed from this level by 1993LiZX   
 81SR2cL actually deexcites the 43/2 member of the band (adopted E=10829 keV).  
 81SR3cL The adopted 1489 keV, 39/2 to 35/2 transition is not reported by       
 81SR4cL 1993LiZX.                                                              
 81SR CL BAND(Q)$|a=-1/2 g{-9/2} band, yrast following crossing of              
 81SR2cL 1-quasiparticle band by this 3-quasiparticle configuration including   
 81SR3cL two aligned g{-9/2} protons.                                           
