 81SR c  Slightly edited dataset of May 13, 2003 (by B. Singh) of SD band data  
 81SR2D  from 2003Le08                                                          
 81SR d  Q data from 1999Le56 for SD-1 added by B. Singh (McMaster), October 25,
 81SR2d  2000                                                                   
 81SR d  Q data from 1997De51 and spin estimated from 1995Ch56 for SD-1 and SD-2
 81SR2d  added by B. Singh (McMaster) June 8, 1999                              
 81SR c  1995Ch56: E=128 MeV; self-supporting enriched target, GAMMASPHERE      
 81SR2c  array (36 Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors) and microball (95 charged 
 81SR3c  particle detectors); measured E|g, I|g, |a(2p)(|g|g|g) coin.           
 81SR4c  Lifetime data analyzed by 1997De51 and transition quadrupole moment    
 81SR5c  deduced for SD-1 and SD-2 bands.                                       
 81SR c  2003Le08, 1999Le56: E=130 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, lifetimes      
 81SR2c  by DSAM using GAMMASPHERE array with 100 Compton-suppressed HPGe       
 81SR3c  detectors and Microball array for charged particles with 95 CsI(Tl)    
 81SR4c  detectors. Deduced SD bands and transition quadrupole moments.         
 81SR cG E         From figure 2 of 1995Ch56; |DE|g?1 keV for highest lying     
 81SR2cG transitions. The evaluator has assigned |DE|g=1. For SD bands, values  
 81SR3cG are from 2003Le08 unless otherwise stated. The corresponding values    
 81SR4cG from 1995Ch56 are generally lower by 2-3 keV.                          
 81SR cG RI        For SD bands: from the intensity pattern shown in fig. 3 of  
 81SR2cG 1995Ch56. Values represent (approximately) percent intensities of the  
 81SR3cG {+81}Sr channel in the reaction used. I|g not stated by authors for    
 81SR4cG other gammas.                                                          
 81SR cL E         From a least-squares fit to E|g, assigning equal weight to   
 81SR2cL all E|g and holding E(level)=79, 132, 366 fixed.                       
 81SR cL E(M)      Level fed by decay of SD band(s).                            
 81SR cL E(E)      Rounded-off energy from Adopted Levels; level not indicated  
 81SR2cL in level scheme in fig. 2 of 1995Ch56, but it must be populated because
 81SR3cL the 79 and 132 levels are populated.                                   
 81SR cL J         From 1995Ch56 for normal deformation states and from         
 81SR2cL 2003Le08 for superdeformed band members, except as noted. Justification
 81SR3cL of J values not given by authors. These values differ from the adopted 
 81SR4cL ones only with regard to the use of parentheses.                       
