 81Y 2cG not M2 from RUL and T{-1/2} (or T{-1/2} limit).                        
 81Y  cL E         From a least-squares fit to E|g, except as noted.            
 81Y  cL E(H)      x>5.3 MeV.                                                   
 81Y  cL E(N)      Member of a |p=(+) sequence of states which feed members of  
 81Y 2cL 5/2[422], |a=+1/2 band. No extended band structure(s) connected with   
 81Y 3cL transitions from these levels could be established (1997Sc17).         
 81Y  cL J         Based on |g(|q) and/or DCO ratio data from                   
 81Y 2cL {+58}Ni({+28}Si,|ap|g), and on intensities and deduced band structure  
 81Y 3cL from {+58}Ni({+28}Si,|ap|g) and {+58}Ni({+32}S,2|ap|g), except as      
 81Y xcL noted.                                                                 
 81Y  cL J(A)      Based on the stronger |e+|b{++} feeding to 3/2+; 5/2+; and   
 81Y 2cL 7/2+ states and weaker feeding to 1/2+ and 3/2- states, authors of     
 81Y 3cL 1985Li12 assign 5/2+ to the {+81}Y parent g.s., presuming              
 81Y 4cL observed population of 1/2+ and 3/2- levels to be indirect, and        
 81Y 5cL ascribing the weaker feeding of 221-keV (3/2+) and 336-keV (5/2+)      
 81Y 6cL levels to inhibition arising from the |DK=2 selection rule.            
 81Y 7cL By contrast, 1982De36 argue that, from level systematics for Z=39 and  
 81Y 8cL even N, the g.s. and first excited state spins should be 1/2- and      
 81Y 9cL 9/2+. Since the latter                                                 
 81Y acL would be excluded by log| {Ift}=5.05 {I3} to (1/2-) (based on their    
 81Y bcL very different decay normalization), they favor a J|p=1/2- parent;     
 81Y ccL 9/2+ is also unlikely since no |e branch is observed to the (9/2+) 132 
 81Y dcL level. However, 1/2- would be tenable only if {+81}Sr J|p assignments  
 81Y ecL from (HI,xn|g) were incorrect. The evaluator adopts (5/2+) from        
 81Y fcL 1985Li12, consistent with energy systematics for 5/2+ states in {+85}Y 
 81Y gcL and {+87}Y. Probable 5/2[422] bandhead (1988Mo17).                     
 81Y  cL J(F)      D |g to (5/2+); |p=- consistent with very small signature    
 81Y 2cL splitting (1985Li12); K|p=3/2- favored by analogy with {+75}Kr (N=39)  
 81Y 3cL and {+83}Y (Z=39). However, K=5/2 has been suggested, based on level   
 81Y 4cL energy systematics within the band as a function of K (1985Li12).      
