 81Y  c  Other: 1993Mi11 (E=120, 125 MeV).                                      
 81Y  c  2002Ka61: E=135 MeV. Measured lifetimes by Doppler-shift attenuation   
 81Y 2c  method using the GAMMASPHERE array (95 Compton-suppressed Ge           
 81Y 3c  detectors and MICROBALL array with 95 CsI(Tl) scintillators).          
 81Y  c  1997Sc17: E=135 MeV, thin target, GAMMASPHERE array (36                
 81Y 2c  Compton-suppressed Ge detectors and 95 CsI-detector microball);        
 81Y 3c  measured E|g, I|g, |g|g|g coin, DCO ratios (unstated); |g energy       
 81Y 4c  resolution<6 keV at 1 MeV after kinematic Doppler-shift correction     
 81Y 5c  had been applied to |g spectrum. Supersedes 1996ScZZ.                  
 81Y  c  1993Mi11: E({+32}S)=120, 125 MeV; 15 or 20                             
 81Y 2c  Compton-suppressed Ge detector array, neutron and |g multiplicity      
 81Y 3c  filter. Measurements were reported along with authors'                 
 81Y 4c  {+58}Ni({+28}Si,|ap|g) reaction work; see ({+28}Si,|ap|g) dataset.     
 81Y  cG E         From 1997Sc17.                                               
 81Y  cG RI        % photon branching from parent level from 2002Ka61;          
 81Y 2cG uncertainty unstated by authors.                                       
 81Y  cL E         From a least-squares fit to E|g.                             
 81Y  cL J         Probable values, deduced by 1997Sc17 from apparent           
 81Y 2cL band structure and unstated DCO ratio data. Data are consistent        
 81Y 3cL with adopted values, but adopted values are shown in parentheses.      
 81Y  cL T         Authors' average of DSAM data at three or four angles        
 81Y 2cL (2002Ka61), corrected for side-feeding unless noted to the contrary.   
 81Y 3cL Values determined from spectra gated from above the transition are     
 81Y 4cL indicated. The authors' model-dependent Q(transition) values           
 81Y 5cL calculated from the measured T{-1/2} data are given in comments.       
 81Y  cL T(A)      Effective half-life (2002Ka61); not corrected for            
 81Y 2cL side-feeding.                                                          
 81Y  cL E(B)      x>5.3 MeV.                                                   
 81Y  cL E(N)      Member of a |p=(+) sequence of states which feed members of  
 81Y 2cL 5/2[422], |a=+1/2 band. No extended band structure(s) connected with   
 81Y 3cL transitions from these levels could be established by 1997Sc17.        
 81Y  CL BAND(O)$|p=(+) band. This band populates the 25/2+ and 29/2+ members   
 81Y 2cL of g.s. band. From |g|g coin and intensity balances, 1997Sc17 deduce   
 81Y 3cL that bandhead for this band lies above the 5265-keV 29/2+ member of the
 81Y 4cL g.s. band, but could not identify transition(s) which connect(s) to    
 81Y 5cL that band.                                                             
 81Y  CL BAND(P)$|p=+, |a=-1/2 band. Possibly approaching termination near      
 81Y 2cL highest J observed.                                                    
