 81Y  c  Other: 1994RaZV                                                        
 81Y  c  Includes {+58}Ni({+28}Si,3p2n|g) (1985Li12).                           
 81Y  c  1985Li12: E({+28}Si)=80-130 MeV, enriched {+58}Ni thick target and     
 81Y 2c  Pb-backed target, LEPS detector (8 angles, |q=0|'-90|'), Ge detector   
 81Y 2c  (8 angles, 90|'-138|'), NE213 scintillator (n detection),              
 81Y 3c  Si telescope at 0|' (|a, p detection); measured                        
 81Y 4c  E|g, I|g, |g|g and particle-|g coin, |g(|q) at E=95 MeV.               
 81Y  c  1993Mi11: E({+28}Si)=100 MeV; 15 or 20                                 
 81Y 2c  Compton-suppressed Ge detector array, neutron and |g multiplicity      
 81Y 3c  filter.                                                                
 81Y  c  1994Jo12: E({+28}Si)=95 MeV; 99.8% {+58}Ni target backed with Ta, six  
 81Y 2c  Compton-suppressed detectors; measured E|g, I|g, |g|g coin, DCO ratios 
 81Y 3c  (|q=0|' and 90|'), T{-1/2} (from DSA or recoil distance Doppler shift).
 81Y  c  1994RaZV: {+28}Si({+58}Ni,|ap|g),                                      
 81Y 2c  E({+58}Ni)=195 MeV; 99.6% enriched {+28}Si target; 20                  
 81Y 3c  Compton-suppressed Ge detectors in rings at 40|', 101|', 117|', 143|'; 
 81Y 4c  measured E|g, I|g (unreported), recoil-|g and |g|g coin, DCO ratios.   
 81Y 5c  {+58}Ni({+28}Si,|ap|g), E({+28}Si)=95 MeV; 99.98%-enriched {+58}Ni     
 81Y 6c  target on Ta backing; 6 Compton-suppressed Ge detectors at 90|', one   
 81Y 7c  HPGe detector at 0|'; measured |g|g coin, DCO ratios, Doppler-broadened
 81Y 8c  lineshapes of short-lived states.                                      
 81Y  cG E         From 1994Jo12, except as noted. E|g values in 1985Li12 are,  
 81Y 2cG typically, quoted to significantly higher precision than those in      
 81Y 3cG 1994Jo12, but fewer lines were observed, so those data are given in    
 81Y 3cG comments; however, a comparison of the 1985Li12 data with those from   
 81Y 4cG 1994Jo12 indicates that E(155|g) from 1985Li12 is significantly low and
 81Y 5cG data from 1985Li12 tend to be higher than those from 1994Jo12 for E|g  
 81Y 6cG above about 300 keV. Also, considering the 1985Li12 data alone, the    
 81Y 7cG 414|g datum is 4|s from the least-squares adjusted value. Possibly the 
 81Y 8cG precision estimates in 1985Li12 are a little optimistic. It should be  
 81Y 9cG noted that E|g data from the {+58}Ni({+32}S,2|ap|g) reaction are       
 81Y acG frequently significantly lower than data from 1994Jo12 or 1985Li12 at  
 81Y bcG the higher energies. |DE is not stated by 1993Mi11; however E|g from   
 81Y ccG 1993Mi11 deviate from those of 1994Jo12 by as much as 3 keV for some   
 81Y dcG lines reported in both studies.                                        
 81Y  cG E(A)      From 1993Mi11; not reported in summary of measured           
 81Y 2cG properties for transitions in |p=+ 5/2[422] band given in table 1 of   
 81Y 3cG 1994Jo12. Not confirmed in subsequent ({+32}S,2|ap|g) study which      
 81Y 4cG extended band to much higher energy than in 1994Jo12.                  
 81Y  cG RI        Intensity relative to I(150|g)=100.0; from ({+28}Si,|ap|g)   
 81Y 2cG at E=95 MeV (1994Jo12), except as noted. 1985Li12 report I|g (without  
 81Y 3cG uncertainties, apparently at same energy), but agreement with 1994Jo12 
 81Y 4cG is poor and those data are not listed here. 1985Li12 also report photon
 81Y 5cG branching from many levels. These values are given in comments on the  
 81Y 6cG relevant gammas; some are of higher precision than I|g from            
 81Y 7cG 1994Jo12 and, except for the 268 and 827 levels, consistency between   
 81Y 8cG branching data from 1985Li12 and 1994Jo12 is good. 1993Mi11 do not     
 81Y 9cG report I|g data.                                                       
 81Y  cG M         From measured DCO ratio (1994Jo12) and/or |g(|q) (1985Li12)  
 81Y 2cG (as listed in comment on relevant transition). Theoretical DCO         
 81Y 3cG values are 1.0 for |DJ=2 and |DJ=0, |?0.45 for stretched D.            
 81Y  cL J         From 1994Jo12, based on measured DCO ratios and deduced      
 81Y 2cL band structure. |p for the proposed |p=- bands is based on             
 81Y 3cL systematics in neighboring isotones. Values differ from                
 81Y 4cL those adopted only with regard to use of parentheses for all adopted   
 81Y 5cL J|p.                                                                   
 81Y  cL E         From a least-squares fit to E|g. The values differ           
 81Y 2cL from those suggested in 1994Jo12 by |<0.3 keV.                         
 81Y  cL T         From DSA measurements (1994Jo12), except as noted, apart from
 81Y 2cL T{-1/2} for 839.34 keV level which is from recoil distance Doppler     
 81Y 3cL shift (1994Jo12).                                                      
 81Y  cL E(A)      Level not adopted because this band                          
