 81MO5c  Identification of {+81}Mo nuclei was made on the basis of magnetic     
 81MO6c  rigidity, time-of-flight and energy loss (tof-B|r-|DE method) of the   
 81MO7c  fragments using BigRIPS fragment separator, atomic number Z of fragment
 81MO8c  by tof and |DE, and A/Q (atomic mass/charge state) of fragment by B|r  
 81MO9c  and tof. Time-of-flight was measured using thin plastic                
 81MOAc  scintillators, |DE by MUSIC ionization chambers, and B|r by particle   
 81MOBc  trajectory reconstructions. Experiments were performed at              
 81MOCc  RIBF-RIKEN facility. Measured A/Q versus Z distributions, deduced      
 81MODc  production cross sections. Theoretical calculations were performed     
 81MOEc  using fission model based LISE** code, and empirical calculations      
 81MOFc  were made using EPAX3.01 and EPAX2.15 codes.                           
 81MO c  2017Su26 (same facility and research group) also reports the same.     
